    "https://guilford.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/US-NC-Greensboro/Part-Time-Choir-Director_JR1340": {
      "title": "Part-Time Choir Director",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPeople are drawn to Guilford College for a number of reasons, including the College’s   Core Values   of community, diversity, equality, excellence, integrity, justice, and stewardship. Working at Guilford provides you with a rewarding opportunity to impact the developing lives of  students from a range of diverse backgrounds . Guilford attracts those who are seeking a professional challenge and career advancement. It also attracts those who want to enjoy a beautiful campus and location in the dynamic city of  Greensboro, North Carolina . Guilford College offers a wide range of benefits for full-time regular employees, including 13 paid holidays, tuition remission, health insurance, telemedicine, life insurance, short-term and long-term disability, a retirement plan, and optional dental and vision insurance. In addition, employment at the College provides employees with access to numerous discounts for products, services, and attractions. Position Summary Guilford College is seeking a Director of the College Choir for the 2027-28 Academic year, with employment beginning in January for the Spring 2027 semester. This appointment is a part-time instructor position. The director will have a firm foundation in classical training as well as experience with a diversity of repertoire in the field of choral music. The director will organize and lead the College Choir which rehearses twice weekly and performs a concert at the end of both the Fall and Spring semesters, as well as at the spring commencement ceremony. The ensemble traditionally includes both college music majors and non-majors, as well as high school students from the Early College at Guilford. The ideal candidate will have experience working with vocalists of a range of ages and abilities , while taking an active role working with the student Choir Officers in recruiting choir members from the campus community. We seek a dynamic and vibrant artist to lead our diverse group of musicians and continue the long tradition of the Guilford College Choir. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Direct the Guilford College Choir (75 minute rehearsals, twice weekly) Participate in choir recruitment efforts as appropriate for a part-time position. Produce a fall concert in collaboration with the other music department ensembles (December). Produce a spring concert (April). Preferred Qualifications A master’s degree in music preferred with an emphasis in choral conducting or voice, or significant professional experience. Teaching experience at the collegiate level Experience with a diversity of choral repertoire  Guilford College does not discriminate on the basis of sex/gender, race, color, creed, religion, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, disability, genetic information, military status, veteran status, or any other protected category under applicable local, state or federal law, ordinance or regulation. See our   full Statement of Non-Discrimination ."
    },
